WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:06.480
The Bureau won't be pursuing you for the matter this time.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.990
Pinning it entirely on Sasano Hiroyuki and me is the easiest way to deal with this case.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.610
The only thing you'll get out of this is their scorn.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.120
Good to hear. I've already earned my fair share of that.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.460
I really do wish I could tell you more.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.880
But alas, I'm sure the future I've seen is meaningless.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.750
Why do you say that?

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.880
You're going to be involved in something big...

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.260
Something involving my successor.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.010
Does such a person exist?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.720
The Bureau has been looking for one for a long time now.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.770
But no matter how much they looked, they couldn't find anyone with the ability to see the future.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:48.900
However,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.400
you know someone who does possess it.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.200
You've met that person a little over two years ago.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.820
Is your successor...

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.790
Is the future-seeing ability user a girl?

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:01.790
Yes.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.420
A slender girl with short hair, big eyes,
and about the age of a middle schooler.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:08.670
Yes.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.170
Is it the girl who died two years ago?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.590
Correct. And you will run into her again.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.880
Haruki, save.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.850
Save.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:24.300
First Time
Saturday, 12:00 PM
August 12th

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.470
It's August 12th, noon sharp.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.100
First Time
Saturday, 12:00 PM
August 12th

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.700
How beautiful.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.580
If you would, please.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.420
Whole body, reset.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.710
Haruki, it's time to reset.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:56.840
Reset.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.500
Saturday, 12:00 PM
August 12th

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.840
It's August 12th, noon sharp.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.670
Second Time

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.840
Saturday, 12:00 PM
August 12th

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.720
We reset, Murase.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.520
I really wanted this petal.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.150
Isn't it just going to disappear soon?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:17.020
The effect of Mr. Sasano's ability lasts ten minutes.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:20.860
The world created by his ability disappears after that.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.610
But I'm sure this petal won't.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:25.530
Why's that?

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.120
Because Mr. Sasano's ability isn't at play here.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.580
The act of using his ability itself

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.790
was erased by our reset.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.000
His ability was never used to begin with,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.210
so there's no reason for the petal to disappear from our world.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.970
I'm going to bring Souma Sumire back to life this way.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.930
Is that possible?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.180
I can't say for sure.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.310
But if this petal doesn't disappear, the same should go for her.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.850
Do you have a picture of her?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.060
Yeah.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.070
It's August 12th, 12:09:50.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.740
Eight...

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.780
Seven...

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.780
Six...

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.660
Five...

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.820
Four...

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:07.660
Three...

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.030
Two...

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.160
One...

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.790
<i>The first time I experienced a reset was during my sixth grade summer vacation.</i>

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.820
Is it broken?

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.150
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.150
I'll fix it for you.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.320
I have the perfect ability for this.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.280
Ability?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.210
There you go.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.670
Make sure you go home before it gets too dark outside.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:11.510
<i>I learned that the denizens of Sakurada all had mysterious abilities.</i>

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.140
<i>The supposedly unbreakable rules of the world</i>

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:18.440
<i>were getting broken so easily it felt like a dream.</i>

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.310
<i>What nagged at me most of all</i>

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.440
<i>was how the existence of such a mysterious city was unknown to the world.</i>

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.030
<i>The denizens of Sakurada made no effort to even try and hide their abilities.</i>

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.660
<i>The reason for that was very interesting.</i>

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:38.500
<i>Anyone who sets foot outside of Sakurada forgets everything about its abilities.</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.080
<i>Without leaving a single trace.</i>

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.800
<i>If forgetting them introduces any inconsistencies, the memories simply change.</i>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>I printed out a map of Sakurada and,
using the information I had gathered,</i>

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:54.560
<i>tried to draw the boundaries where you lose your memories.</i>

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.940
<i>That's when it hit me.</i>

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.990
<i>My memories were extremely vivid—
to an unbelievable degree.</i>

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:14.580
<i>I was able to remember everything I'd ever come across</i>

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.000
<i>in painstaking detail that I was sure was impossible for humans.</i>

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.580
<i>That was my ability.</i>

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.760
You are Asai Kei, correct?

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.090
Who are you?

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.590
We are from the Bureau.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.220
The Bureau?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.930
It's a public organization that oversees all the abilities in Sakurada.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.060
How did you find out?

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.190
I do not understand your question.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:48.690
Could you tell me how you found out about my ability?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.200
I am not allowed to answer your question.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.910
I see.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.370
Could you at least tell me your name?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.580
That is also a matter I am not allowed to disclose.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.910
That sounds pretty inconvenient.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.960
What do people usually call you?

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.420
Index.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.170
Miss Index...

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:14.390
The Bureau has come to one conclusion regarding you.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.180
Which is?

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:18.180
You are not allowed to leave Sakurada.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.770
Why?

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.730
I am not allowed to answer your question.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.060
Well, I more or less get the picture.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.860
They oversee all the abilities in Sakurada,

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.110
and mine is problematic for them.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.030
That means it's related to the fundamental rules of the abilities,

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.360
which basically spells it out.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.580
If I leave Sakurada, I won't lose my memories about its abilities.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.580
What leads you to believe that?

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.880
I can't think of any other possibility.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.840
Very well.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.550
You are correct.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:54.340
In any event, the Bureau wants to form a contract with you.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.590
You have no say in the matter.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:01.720
The Bureau will assure your livelihood in Sakurada.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.640
And in exchange, you will remain in Sakurada

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.810
and will not tell anyone about this agreement.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:11.400
And finally, the Bureau will purchase your past.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.900
For a healthy sum of money, at that.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.320
Purchase my past?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.870
Do you mean, like, they'll fake my death or something?

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.160
No. To be more precise,

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.080
your existence itself will be erased.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:29.840
So my parents will forget all about me?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.170
Yes, as painful as that must be for you.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.340
No, that's just what I want.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:54.940
Sakurada City Bureau

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.620
Is it broken?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.130
I'll fix it for you.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.210
I have the perfect ability for this.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.680
What a useful ability.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.350
I guess.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:26.060
If only I could mend the human heart with it,

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.600
I'd have no complaints.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.480
You're asking a bit much there.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.810
Maybe so.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.150
Make sure you go home before it gets too dark outside.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.130
<i>That day, I threw away my past.</i>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:05.890
Hey...

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.980
Hey, you!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.400
Are you crying?

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:15.820
Why would you think that?

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.200
I figured it'd make you answer me.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:37.500
Yes?

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.220
Haruki, save.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.680
First Time
Monday, 06:20 PM
August 28th
Save.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.470
It's August 18th, 6:20 p.m.
August 28th
Monday, 06:20 PM
First Time

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:50.020
I'm thinking about going to Sakagami to see if he'll help us.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.560
Since you just had me save,

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.400
does that mean you want him to forget what happens?

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.360
Most likely, yeah.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.650
I think that's for the best.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.650
Kei.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.410
Since I'm here right now,

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.660
that means it's for the best if I'm not there too, right?

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.700
Sorry.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.830
There's no need to apologize.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.960
I'll follow your orders.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.290
No matter what they are.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.080
Thanks.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.500
See you later.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.170
See you.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.550
<i>Thinking back on it,</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.930
<i>there have been hints all along.</i>

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.310
Hey, Kei.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.650
Hey, Tomoki.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.110
I saw Souma yesterday.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.070
She swung by around noon.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.820
She wanted me to send a message to the future.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.820
To herself, in two years.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:49.620
To herself two years in the future?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.450
Yeah.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.960
But now that she's dead,
there's no way she'll ever get it.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.670
What did she say?

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.040
Hm?

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:00.340
What did she want to tell herself two years later?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.090
"Can you hear me?"

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.380
That's all.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:09.350
First Time
Wednesday
August 30th

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:14.690
The last time I saved was August 28th, 6:20 p.m.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.900
That's exactly two days ago.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:17.730
Right.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.230
Do you think it'll work?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.610
Yeah.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:26.200
It's already been determined this plan will work.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.240
All we need to do is follow the script.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.080
What script?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:35.080
Souma had the ability to see the future.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.500
Does that mean she already knew what would happen that summer?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.800
I think we should assume she knew everything.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:50.100
She foresaw everything that has happened from the very beginning.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:54.350
She knew that we'd become friends on that rooftop.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.850
And I'm sure this thing is no exception.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.900
The MacGuffin?

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.480
I'm willing to bet it's just an ordinary stone.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.070
One talked up by Souma Sumire's rumor.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:08.240
An object that serves merely as a trigger for the protagonist's story.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:13.370
To put it one way, the MacGuffin is just a stage prop meant to kick the story into its rising action.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.500
"Its owner will be able to control all the abilities in Sakurada."

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.000
The effect of that rumor was tremendous.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.630
An ordinary black stone became the MacGuffin

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.590
and led me to a lot of ability users.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.090
Murase Youka.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:28.840
Sasano Hiroyuki.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.970
Sakagami Yousuke.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.220
And...

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.470
you, Haruki.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.860
That's probably the only thing this stone was supposed to do.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:46.320
It was just a prop to bring together all the actors

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.400
necessary for the story of Souma Sumire's revival.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:51.870
Kei.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.200
You seem happy for some reason.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.620
I get the feeling a question that's been bothering me for a long time will soon be answered.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.420
But at the same time, you seem somehow sad.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.960
The answer I've been long waiting for

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.800
might actually be something very sad.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.640
What is that question?

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.640
"Why did Souma Sumire die?"

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.270
She could see the future.
There's no way she'd die in an accident.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:27.320
Haruki, do you remember that android thing?

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.030
Souma Sumire's question?

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:30.900
Yeah.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.910
She was talking about herself.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:38.910
She saw the future, made a plan,
and acted according to that program.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.830
Even if that meant throwing away her life in the process.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.710
Kei, I have a question.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:51.090
Is the girl inside the photograph actually Souma Sumire?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:55.220
Will we really be able to say we revived her

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.680
if we drag her out of a photograph?

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.230
Are you thinking about Kurakawa Mari?

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.190
Yes.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:06.940
The girl cloned with an ability to perfectly resemble Kurakawa Mari

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.690
made her mother doubt and suffer because she wasn't the same being.

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:13.450
So what's the deal with the
Souma Sumire inside the photograph?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.070
Is she like the Swampman you talked about?

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.750
I wouldn't know.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:21.410
But you know what, Haruki?

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.960
It doesn't matter if she's the same person or someone else.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.000
I think we should just pray for the happiness that comes from this.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.590
I am worried, though.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.510
We're reviving a dead person,

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.560
and someone with the ability to see the future at that.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:44.600
I can't imagine her newfound life will be peaceful.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.440
I...

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:50.070
I know all about the woman who lost her very name and took up the name "Witch."

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.530
I'm sure Souma even knew I'd get worried about this.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:59.870
That's why in that picture she's holding out the MacGuffin.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.000
Like she's telling me to accept this script.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.630
I'll drag Souma out of the photograph.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.670
That's what I decided.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:12.840
I understand.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.380
Oh, you're here early.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.100
Good evening, Murase.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.470
And thanks for coming, Sakagami.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.230
You don't have to thank me.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.850
I'll do anything to help bring Souma back to life.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.610
Never would've guessed this sort of roundabout way existed.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.150
I'm sorry.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.200
It's fine.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.490
It's not like we can do anything about it.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.700
We can't exactly go to the past and have my brother's picture taken, can we?

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.750
Still, I'm sorry.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.380
Yeah, I get it. Let's do this thing already.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.760
Is everyone ready?

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.510
Let's start.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.130
Three...

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:57.880
Two...

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:58.970
One...

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.140
We're inside the photograph.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.410
You're not going?

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:27.790
No.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.250
I'll have a nice chat with her later.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.340
It's really Souma!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.840
C'mon, get to it.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.170
R-Right.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.300
Excuse me for a moment.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.050
You can start.

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:44.930
Whole body. Reset.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.310
Good to go!

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:49.190
Haruki, it's time to reset.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.190
Reset.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.780
Thank you very much.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.000
Hello, Kei.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.960
Hello.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:15.550
I guess "Long time no see" doesn't exactly apply to you.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.340
Guess so.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:21.390
From where I stand, I saw you three days ago.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.550
When was that?

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:28.430
Mari's mother tried to leave Sakurada three days ago to me.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.600
I see.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.770
You've gotten a lot taller.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.320
Kind of surprised me.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.490
I used to be on the shorter side.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.860
Now I'm pretty much the class average.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:43.870
I see.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:46.910
How have you been these past two years?

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.620
I've been getting along.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.370
All kinds of things have happened.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.170
Both ups and downs.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.840
Did you become friends with Haruki?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.340
We're definitely much closer than two years ago, yes.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.010
She's changed.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.090
She's become a very normal girl.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.050
And I'm sure she'll keep changing.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.600
I see.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.930
Are you fine with that, Kei?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:12.190
Of course.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.020
I think it's a very good thing.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.900
But you fell in love with the girl she was two years ago, right?

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.780
She was as simple as they come

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.860
and had no sense of self.

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.950
She was basically the incarnation of pure virtue,

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.330
and that's why you fell in love with her, right?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.370
I wonder about that...

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:34.960
I'm sure you've been through a lot and have grown pretty strong.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.790
I couldn't say if I've gotten stronger,

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:41.010
but I think I've changed in some ways.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:41.800
Like how?

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:47.010
I probably wouldn't turn down a girl who invites me to see the sunset with her.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.260
Even if you have a book to finish?

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:50.220
Yeah.

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:57.020
There are two things I'd like to ask you.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.150
What might they be?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:04.200
Two years ago, you set up a message to yourself through Tomoki's ability.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.070
A message saying, "Can you hear me?"

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.910
So I did. What of it?

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:12.330
I didn't actually catch when it was supposed to be delivered.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.920
What time did you set it for?

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:18.340
I had him set it for today at 6:30 p.m.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:20.050
In five minutes or so, I believe.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.880
I see.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:27.180
If I'm Souma Sumire, Nakano's ability will deliver the message to me.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.390
If I don't hear it, it'll mean I'm someone else who just looks like her.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.310
What's your other question?

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:36.020
Why did you die?

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:41.360
She had a reason that left her no choice but to die.

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.820
A reason that forced her to die?

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:46.450
Exactly.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:51.450
A reason she had to kill herself so quietly,
like it was an accident.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:53.790
But you're here now.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.210
Just like you planned.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.710
It was all necessary.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:01.920
Souma Sumire dying, and me, her exact clone, being born.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:02.920
Why?

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.460
That's a secret.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.590
Let me keep it a secret for a bit longer.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:13.220
Feel free to hate me.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:16.270
I did more than enough to deserve it.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:19.690
You're right. You crossed the line.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.230
I'm sorry.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.820
Even if I hurt you,

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:27.490
and even if I might do it again in the future,

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:29.490
there's something I just can't give up on.

00:22:31.490 --> 00:22:32.490
You know, Kei.

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:38.620
I wanted to make you the protagonist of the story I cooked up.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.840
Everything that happened up to now was in preparation for that.

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:45.260
What's this story you cooked up?

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:48.510
You already know that.

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:53.010
The owner of the MacGuffin will control all the abilities in Sakurada.

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:05.530
It's time.

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:08.740
Did you hear your voice?

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:10.990
Good question.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:14.990
What do you want the answer to be?

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:24.460
I'm sure whichever one you choose is correct.

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:33.760
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:41.230
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:41.850 --> 00:23:46.690
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:54.780
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:23:55.700 --> 00:24:00.370
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:07.550
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:12.050
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:15.430
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:21.430
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:28.570
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:35.070
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:35.070 --> 00:24:42.250
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:46.330
You're the one who brought it back

00:24:46.330 --> 00:24:53.170
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful

00:24:55.970 --> 00:24:57.470
Next Episode

00:24:57.470 --> 00:24:59.600
Now we can text each other and hold long phone calls.

00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:01.390
There's no connection between colds and love.

00:25:01.390 --> 00:25:02.270
That's impossible.

00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:04.140
Yeah, rice porridge just has to be with dried plums.

00:25:04.140 --> 00:25:04.980
Now that's a problem.

00:25:04.980 --> 00:25:07.110
I wonder if this will make Kei happy.

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:09.820
Will you be my friend?
